FastCGI transport: coalesce record headers and large response bodies with writev()

Large response chunks bypass the output buffer to avoid copying, but the record
header and body were written with separate write() calls. In optimized transport
mode on Unix, send both with writev() while retaining the existing path for the
classic transport and Windows.

The helper handles EINTR and partial writes across both vectors. This preserves
the FastCGI byte stream while reducing write syscalls for a 256 KB response from
11 to 6.

